  "description": "VEGYEO crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C140 H102 Ce3 Mn8 O48,C1 H3 N1 O2,0.5(C1 H2 Cl2),0.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn8 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 26 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.148-4.057 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.38-126.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce3Mn8O8(O2CPh)18(HO2CPh)2]·x(solvent).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
